WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.301
Now it's being compared to

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.836
finding a needle in a haystack.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.170
But imagine if that needle

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.972
were highly radioactive.

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:06.506
Well, search

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.308
crews scanning a remote highway

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.442
in Australia

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:10.243
actually managed

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.946
to find this tiny radioactive capsule

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.181
after it was missing for six days.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.317
It's the size of a small coin

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.184
and appears

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.053
to have fallen off the back of a trans

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.121
port truck.

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.989
Crews looking for it

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.758
combed an area roughly

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:27.460
the length of the UK

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:29.162
When you consider

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.464
the scope of the research area,

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.532
locating this object

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.768
was a monumental challenge.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:35.502
The search crews

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.470
have quite literally found

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.106
the needle in the haystack.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.374
CNN correspondent Mark Stewart

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.009
joins us live from Hong Kong.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:43.843
Great news,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.011
an extraordinary effort

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.746
as well in this search.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:47.313
Indeed, back

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:47.881
so the story is

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:50.450
just so intriguing for some reason.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.185
Let me give you some context.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.821
This is a Hong Kong coin.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:57.690
It's very similar in size to a US dime.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.625
It is that small.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:00:59.659
I want to make sure you can see it

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.161
here of the skyline.

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.162
Basically,

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.129
this capsule that was

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.432
found is used for mining.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.366
Here's the history.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.000
The capsule

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:07.700
was discovered

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.334
about six

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.202
days, six days

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:11.071
after it went missing,

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.773
likely falling off a truck.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:14.641
Now, eventually,

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.743
it was found off the side of a road

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:17.377
by crews

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.079
who are using special radiation

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.947
detection equipment.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.650
It was not found too far from the Rio

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.451
Tinto mine

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.686
suggesting it fell off the truck

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.922
soon as it left.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.191
But the potential search area for

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.326
this was enormous. Vast.

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.728
You mentioned the size of the U.K.,

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:36.963
I believe

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.832
we are talking about distance here

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:41.568
longer than the California coastline.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.369
A perimeter was set up.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.972
And so now the goal is to transport

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.508
this capsule in a lead container

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:51.111
to the health department to a facility

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.846
they have in Perth.

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:54.114
But this was very concerning

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.149
because human exposure could cause

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:57.450
skin burns,

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.785
radiation sickness,

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:01.421
even a risk of cancer in some cases.

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:04.591
And just 24 hours ago, authorities felt

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.892
that the chance of finding

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.694
it was very slim.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:08.461
Now, Max,

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.530
they have to determine how this happened

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.364
in the first place,

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:13.700
how it fell off that truck likely.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:14.801
Okay, Mark.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.169
Sure. It's fascinating Thank you.

